â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â• */
/* ROOT CAUSE of "sidebar width never visibly changes": this compound
   selector (body.dark-mode .orv-sb) has higher specificity than the plain
   .orv-sb rule above, so its own !important width (200px, then 176px in
   the "V2 NAV ADJUSTMENTS" block further below) silently won over every
   previous width edit whenever the app was in dark mode -- completely
   independent of what the base rule said. Width aligned to the shared
   280px target. Background is near-black and only subtly lighter than
   .mc's own near-black (#070707) -- deliberately close, not a strong
   color contrast; the border below is what actually delineates the two. */
body.dark-mode .orv-sb {
  background: #0B0B0C !important;
  border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06) !important;
  width: 280px !important;
  min-width: 280px !important;
