   aligned below the list, only rendered once items exist (bizRenderList,
   app.html) — the empty state already carries its own single CTA. */
.biz-add-btn-trailing { margin-top: 12px; align-self: flex-end; }
.biz-vcard-list + .biz-add-btn-trailing { margin-top: 12px; }

/* ══ Navbar Redesign — command rail ════════════════════════════════
   Existing .orv-sb has THREE separate `width:280px !important` rules
   scattered across the file's history (base block, two dark-mode
   blocks). Rather than track all of them down, these overrides are
   appended here (verified-safe location this session — see the earlier
   Business/Autopilot content-width fixes for why) with matching
   !important + equal specificity, so they win purely on being last in
   source order. .mc (main content) is flex:1 in the same flex row, so
   narrowing .orv-sb hands the freed space to page content automatically
   — no separate content-width edit needed. */
.orv-sb {
  width: 220px !important;
  min-width: 220px !important;
  max-width: 220px !important;
  border-radius: 0 16px 16px 0 !important;
  border-right: 1px solid var(--b2, rgba(0,0,0,.1)) !important;
  box-shadow: 4px 0 24px -8px rgba(0,0,0,.12) !important;
  position: relative !important;
}
body.dark-mode .orv-sb {
  width: 220px !important;
  min-width: 220px !important;
  border-radius: 0 16px 16px 0 !important;
  border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06) !important;
  box-shadow: 4px 0 28px -8px rgba(0,0,0,.5) !important;
}

/* Logo — more breathing room, still the same asset/markup. */
.orv-sb-logo { padding: 22px 18px 18px !important; gap: 12px !important; }

/* Nav items — trimmed a touch for the narrower rail; active state stays
   the existing subtle green-tint + left accent bar (already restrained,
