.orv-ni-plat-dot-off { background: var(--b2, rgba(0,0,0,.18)); }
.orv-ni-plat-ext { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); flex-shrink: 0; opacity: .7; }

/* Mobile drawer reuses .orv-ni-plat-group/.orv-ni-plat as-is — slightly
   more vertical padding to match the drawer's own larger touch targets. */
.orv-mob-drawer .orv-ni-plat-group { margin-left: 10px; }
.orv-mob-drawer .orv-ni-plat { padding: 8px 10px; min-height: 36px; }

/* ══ Autopilot Alignment Pass ══════════════════════════════════════
   Same root cause already fixed for Intelligence (search this file for
   "#page-intelligence .ov3-section"): .ov3-section (shared by
   apEngineSection/apSourcesSection/apActiveSection/apHistorySection)
   carries its own 32px (48px dark) left/right padding on top of
   .ap-op-outer's own page padding, and in dark mode a separate
   "Sections below hero also centered" rule additionally applies
   max-width:800px + margin:0 auto !important. The Intelligence fix's own
   comment assumed Autopilot's copy of this padding was intentional and
   didn't need the same treatment — a live getBoundingClientRect check
   this pass proved that wrong: hero headline measured x=260 while every
   .ov3-section heading (Automation Engine/Monitoring Sources/Active
   Automations/History) measured x=292, a consistent 32px gap, and in
   dark mode the sections additionally self-centered at 800px regardless
   of the page's real content width. Neutralizing here, scoped to
   #page-autopilot only — .ov3-section's behavior on every other page
   (including Intelligence's own separate override) is untouched. */
#page-autopilot .ov3-section { padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; }
body.dark-mode #page-autopilot .ov3-section { padding-left: 0 !important; padding-right: 0 !important; max-width: none !important; margin-left: 0 !important; margin-right: 0 !important; }

/* ══ Design System Consistency Pass — canonical title/subtitle system ══
   Audit found the shared .orv-ph-title/.orv-ph-sub pair (used by
   Intelligence and Business's page headers, styles.css:25744/25753:
   22px/800/-.03em/1.2 line-height, 13px sub/1.5 line-height) is already
   the most widely-reused primary-title pattern in the app. Two real
   outliers found against it, fixed here rather than touched at their
   original definitions (avoids re-litigating every other rule already
   layered around them):
   - .ap-hero-headline (Autopilot's real title, "Let Oriven handle...")
     was 28px/-.02em — 6px larger than every other page's title, the
     single most visible inconsistency in the audit.
   - .ap-hero-sub was 14px/1.55 vs the canonical 13px/1.5.
   - .camp-shell-title (Campaigns) was already 22px but weight 700/
     letter-spacing -.02em vs canonical 800/-.03em.
   Not touched: .orv-greeting (Overview's own greeting, a different,
   deliberately larger component per section 35's "don't flatten good
   design that serves a different purpose"); section-heading labels
   (.ov3-sh-label, 10.5px/700/.08em) were already consistent everywhere
   they're used (Autopilot/Intelligence/Business) — no fix needed there. */
.ap-hero-headline { font-size: 22px !important; font-weight: 800 !important; letter-spacing: -.03em !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; }
.ap-hero-sub { font-size: 13px !important; line-height: 1.5 !important; }
.camp-shell-title { font-weight: 800 !important; letter-spacing: -.03em !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; }
.camp-shell-sub { line-height: 1.5 !important; }

/* ══ Page Header Alignment Fix ══════════════════════════════════════
   Live Campaigns / Drafts kept their real Refresh / +New Campaign
